{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Missingness Indicator.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Missingness Indicator.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"missingness indicator missingness indicator","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Missingness Indicator.md","fileName":"Missingness Indicator.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Missingness Indicator","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 18:44\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Analytic Data Preparation]] · [[Data Quality and Missing Data]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Analytic Data Preparation","Data Quality and Missing Data","analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf","essentialsofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Missingness Indicator.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Missingness Indicator.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"missingness indicator missingness indicator","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Missingness Indicator.md","fileName":"Missingness Indicator.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Missingness Indicator","heading":"Missingness Indicator","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A missingness indicator is a binary variable that marks whether another variable is absent or contains a code treated as unknown. It makes the distribution of missing information explicit and supports checks against the original field.\n\nThe indicator can help audit exclusions or describe a missing category, but it does not restore the missing measurement. If most outcome-positive records lack a required time value, a flag exposes a severe data limitation that imputation may not credibly solve.\n\nThe book also reviews missingness at the variable level before modeling. Fields that are entirely or largely missing may be excluded or handled explicitly, while rough imputation is reserved for exploratory workflows whose limitations are understood.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Analytic Data Preparation","Data Quality and Missing Data","analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf","essentialsofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Missingness Indicator.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Missingness Indicator.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"missingness indicator missingness indicator","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Missingness Indicator.md","fileName":"Missingness Indicator.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Missingness Indicator","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf]]\n\n[[essentialsofdatascience.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Analytic Data Preparation","Data Quality and Missing Data","analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf","essentialsofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}